<p><a class=cimage href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/2022-05-08-8.png"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/2022-05-08-8.png" alt="" width="840" height="577" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-90604" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/2022-05-08-8.png 2096w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/2022-05-08-8-300x206.png 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/2022-05-08-8-1024x704.png 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/2022-05-08-8-768x528.png 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/2022-05-08-8-1536x1055.png 1536w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/2022-05-08-8-2048x1407.png 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>Whaa&#8230;  it&#8217;s been less than a month since the last of these posts (wherein I give a report from my gamified Emacs bug tracker spelunking).</p>
<p>I&#8217;ve been using various ways to select bug reports to handle since I started on this back in&#8230;  2019?  Yes.  I started, of course, with reports about things that I had experience with (Gnus, eww, etc), but I soon ran out of things to do that way.</p>
<p>So instead I started looking through all bug reports that hadn&#8217;t had any responses, and then all bug reports I had been the last person to respond (they have a tendency to end with &#8220;So I think we should do &lt;foo&gt;, anybody have any comments?&#8221; and then nobody does.  So then I would do &lt;foo&gt;.</p>
<p><a class=cimage href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/2022-05-08-9.png"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/2022-05-08-9.png" alt="" width="840" height="581" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-90605" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/2022-05-08-9.png 2012w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/2022-05-08-9-300x208.png 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/2022-05-08-9-1024x709.png 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/2022-05-08-9-768x532.png 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/2022-05-08-9-1536x1063.png 1536w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>But then I ran out of those, too, so I started just sorting all the bug reports by the length of the discussion.  It looks like this:</p>
<p><a class=cimage href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/2022-04-27.png"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/2022-04-27.png" alt="" width="840" height="991" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-90463" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/2022-04-27.png 1864w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/2022-04-27-254x300.png 254w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/2022-04-27-868x1024.png 868w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/2022-04-27-768x906.png 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/2022-04-27-1301x1536.png 1301w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/2022-04-27-1735x2048.png 1735w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>And this 10% stretch!</p>
<a href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/2022/05/09/16x10/"><img decoding="async" src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/plugins/wp-youtube-lyte/lyteCache.php?origThumbUrl=https%3A%2F%2Fi.ytimg.com%2Fvi%2FaPY4mtT2xfg%2Fhqdefault.jpg" alt="YouTube Video"></a><br /><br />
<p>I made it all of the way to the bottom, Maggie!</p>
<p>The longest bug thread had 135 messages.</p>
<p>It turns out that, contrary to what I had imagined, many of those well-discussed bug reports had actionable conclusions: That is, after discussing something back and forth for a couple of years, the conclusion was that indeed we should do &lt;foo&gt;, but then nobody did.</p>
<p>So I did that now, which explains why this is the speediest ten-percenter in quite a while:</p>
<p><a class=cimage href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/2022-05-08.png"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/2022-05-08.png" alt="" width="840" height="163" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-90594" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/2022-05-08.png 1342w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/2022-05-08-300x59.png 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/2022-05-08-1024x200.png 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/2022-05-08-768x150.png 768w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>Started April 13th, done May 8th.</p>
<p>Of course, reading those threads too some time, but figuring out what to do usually takes more time.</p>
<p>Anyway, that means that there aren&#8217;t really anything big new feature to report this time over (except that Tree Sitter has landed on a feature branch), just a buttload of bug fixes and small new features.  Here&#8217;s some of them:</p>
<h4>Easier Scripting</h4>
<p><a class=cimage href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/2022-05-08-1.png"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/2022-05-08-1.png" alt="" width="627" height="158" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-90596" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/2022-05-08-1.png 627w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/2022-05-08-1-300x76.png 300w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 627px) 100vw, 627px" /></a></p>
<p>Emacs now has an <tt>-x</tt> switch designed to make scripting easier.  With the above, you can do:</p>
<p><a class=cimage href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/2022-05-08-2.png"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/2022-05-08-2.png" alt="" width="755" height="169" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-90597" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/2022-05-08-2.png 755w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/2022-05-08-2-300x67.png 300w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 755px) 100vw, 755px" /></a></p>
<p>Emacs almost had this capability before, but it was a bit messy and not very convenient.</p>
<h4>Restarting Emacs</h4>
<p>When trying stuff out in Emacs, you want to be able to restart Emacs conveniently so that you can see that things work as you want them to.  A new <tt>M-x restart-emacs</tt> command now makes things easier.</p>
<h4>*Help* improvements</h4>
<p>My mission to make the help buffers prettier and easier to read continues, and menus which used to be explained this way&#8230;</p>
<p><a class=cimage href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/2022-05-08-3.png"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/2022-05-08-3.png" alt="" width="840" height="126" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-90598" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/2022-05-08-3.png 1686w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/2022-05-08-3-300x45.png 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/2022-05-08-3-1024x154.png 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/2022-05-08-3-768x115.png 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/2022-05-08-3-1536x230.png 1536w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>&#8230; are now displayed this way:</p>
<p><a class=cimage href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/2022-05-08-4.png"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/2022-05-08-4.png" alt="" width="840" height="149" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-90599" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/2022-05-08-4.png 1656w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/2022-05-08-4-300x53.png 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/2022-05-08-4-1024x182.png 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/2022-05-08-4-768x136.png 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/2022-05-08-4-1536x273.png 1536w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>You can now also edit variable values, and you can keep the *Help* window selected (without popping to other windows when clicking on buttons in that window).</p>
